## 12. Lasso Feature Selection Results

The tuned 48-feature model used L1 regularization.

| Feature Selection Metric | Result |
|---|---:|
| Total Input Features | 48 |
| Selected Features | 32 |
| Eliminated Features | 16 |
| Selected Percentage | 66.7% |
| Eliminated Percentage | 33.3% |
| Best Alpha | 0.01 |

Lasso automatically assigned zero coefficients to 16 predictors.

The remaining 32 predictors had nonzero coefficients.

Pythagorean Expected Wins was one of the retained features.

**Interpretation:** Lasso attempts to retain a useful combination of predictors while penalizing model complexity. Features receiving zero coefficients are not necessarily useless individually; they may be redundant given the other variables.

